1
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:01,187
Where do you think you're going

2
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,938
without my final approval?

3
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:07,485
I won't let you quit.

4
00:01:15,951 --> 00:01:18,871
Do you think she'll treat you
better than I do?

5
00:01:18,954 --> 00:01:19,830
You think so?

6
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:22,166
Do you really think so?

7
00:01:22,249 --> 00:01:23,209
Are you sure?

8
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:26,295
-Excuse me, Mr. Yoon.
-Mr. Yoon?

9
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:28,881
Hey.

10
00:01:31,884 --> 00:01:33,385
How long have you been here?

11
00:01:33,469 --> 00:01:35,554
What brings you here out of the blue?

12
00:01:40,893 --> 00:01:41,894
Look for him.

13
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:47,733
You have five minutes.

14
00:01:47,817 --> 00:01:49,068
-Five minutes? Go!
-Hurry.

15
00:01:49,151 --> 00:01:50,444
-Hurry!
-We have five minutes!

16
00:01:50,528 --> 00:01:51,570
-Hurry!
-Move it!

17
00:01:51,654 --> 00:01:54,031
-Notify it on the group chat too.
-Please, miss.

18
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,534
I've never been able to bring her
somewhere like this.

19
00:01:57,576 --> 00:02:01,247
It's her birthday today.
She wants to ride the attractions.

20
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:03,082
I'm sincerely sorry, sir.

21
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:06,877
We stop admitting guests
30 minutes before closing.

22
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:08,796
I understand.

23
00:02:13,801 --> 00:02:15,261
That's mine.

24
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,017
Here.

25
00:02:22,893 --> 00:02:24,436
-Son.
-Thank you.

26
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:25,688
Dad!

27
00:02:27,231 --> 00:02:30,192
I told you not to run
when there are a lot of people, son.

28
00:02:30,276 --> 00:02:31,360
"Son"?

29
00:02:40,286 --> 00:02:41,370
"Dad"?

30
00:02:46,542 --> 00:02:48,043
Who are you, mister?

31
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:52,548
And who are you?

32
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:54,008
Do you know my dad?

33
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:56,260
Are you Kang Jae-hee's son?

34
00:02:56,343 --> 00:02:57,928
I asked you first.

35
00:02:58,012 --> 00:02:59,388
I'm more curious than you are.

36
00:03:00,973 --> 00:03:04,351
Dad, this man talks funny.

37
00:03:05,144 --> 00:03:08,022
What did I tell you to do

38
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:10,232
when you see a stranger?

39
00:03:10,316 --> 00:03:12,443
I shouldn't follow them.

40
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,654
But it sounds like he knows you.

41
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:18,407
-Is he also a police--
-Your mom must be waiting.

42
00:03:19,283 --> 00:03:20,618
-What?
-Let's go to her.

43
00:03:20,701 --> 00:03:22,077
-Okay.
-Let's go!

44
00:03:22,161 --> 00:03:24,496
-Okay.
-Let's find Mom!

45
00:03:25,122 --> 00:03:26,081
"Mom"?

46
00:03:27,082 --> 00:03:29,251
Kang Jae-hee! Were you married?

47
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:37,051
Thank you and I'm sorry,
Staff Sergeant Kang.

48
00:03:37,885 --> 00:03:39,094
Jin-hyung is looking

49
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,764
more like Sergeant Go every year.

50
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:45,935
Son.

51
00:03:46,977 --> 00:03:49,396
I hope you're 2 cm taller
the next time I see you.

52
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:51,273
Okay, I promise.

53
00:03:51,357 --> 00:03:52,858
Promise.

54
00:03:55,527 --> 00:03:56,445
What's this?

55
00:03:57,154 --> 00:03:59,073
-Thanks.
-Bye, Dad.

56
00:03:59,156 --> 00:04:01,241
-Bye.
-High five!

57
00:04:01,325 --> 00:04:02,284
High five!

58
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:04,828
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

59
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:15,589
Thanks for hanging out with me, Dad.

60
00:04:15,673 --> 00:04:17,508
Hang out with me next time too!

61
00:04:17,883 --> 00:04:20,636
And I don't think he's a bad man.

62
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,481
Should I ask first,
or will you explain first?

63
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:34,066
I found him!

64
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:35,109
-Sir.
-I found him.

65
00:04:35,192 --> 00:04:37,236
-Wait.
-Why is he here?

66
00:04:37,945 --> 00:04:40,531
Why is he here?

67
00:04:41,490 --> 00:04:42,908
-Sir!
-Sir!

68
00:04:42,992 --> 00:04:44,159
-Sir!
-Where are you going?

69
00:04:44,243 --> 00:04:46,829
I don't want to.
Why would I ride this with you?

70
00:04:46,912 --> 00:04:48,455
Because I want to.

71
00:04:48,539 --> 00:04:50,332
Then you can ride it alone.

72
00:04:50,874 --> 00:04:51,959
Thank you.

73
00:04:53,961 --> 00:04:55,421
Let's go ride it, Mother.

74
00:05:02,094 --> 00:05:05,055
If you've noticed,
then play along with my power trip.

75
00:05:10,728 --> 00:05:12,271
This is unexpected of him.

76
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,274
He could've just told me.

77
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:26,952
During the interview, you told me

78
00:05:27,995 --> 00:05:29,830
your comrade died in front of your eyes.

79
00:05:29,913 --> 00:05:31,290
Is the boy his son?

80
00:05:31,373 --> 00:05:33,250
I don't want to talk
about my personal life.

81
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:35,335
I quit working for you.

82
00:05:36,628 --> 00:05:39,173
Right. As soon as you quit working for me,

83
00:05:39,256 --> 00:05:41,175
you started working for Lee Si-a.

84
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:42,926
That never happened.

85
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,597
I know she lied.

86
00:05:48,182 --> 00:05:50,768
I know better than anyone
that you're not that heartless.

87
00:05:51,769 --> 00:05:53,520
But I needed an excuse to come here

88
00:05:54,229 --> 00:05:55,481
and convince you.

89
00:05:56,565 --> 00:05:58,567
So in conclusion…

90
00:05:58,984 --> 00:06:02,279
You want me to know and handle everything
before you say something?

91
00:06:03,739 --> 00:06:04,740
I'm sorry

92
00:06:05,491 --> 00:06:07,076
for lashing out like that.

93
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:14,208
It was hard for me to accept it
because it was my first time.

94
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:16,335
You're the first person

95
00:06:16,794 --> 00:06:19,088
to break through my walls.

96
00:06:20,756 --> 00:06:23,008
That doesn't mean you can just lash out.

97
00:06:23,092 --> 00:06:25,511
You knew I only did what I did
because I was worried.

98
00:06:25,594 --> 00:06:27,596
What's with you?
Do I look like a pushover?

99
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:31,225
You're the first person
I can't control as I please.

100
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:33,227
And you're saying
I think you're a pushover?

101
00:06:36,939 --> 00:06:37,940
I decided

102
00:06:39,274 --> 00:06:40,776
to accept it.

103
00:06:42,402 --> 00:06:43,654
Kang Jae-hee.

104
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,491
As for me,

105
00:06:48,492 --> 00:06:49,326
I like…

106
00:06:50,077 --> 00:06:50,911
I like…

107
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:53,205
I need you.

108
00:06:54,289 --> 00:06:55,707
I think I need you.

109
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,802
This must be

110
00:07:07,302 --> 00:07:08,637
a surprise inspection, right?

111
00:07:11,306 --> 00:07:14,560
Let's show him
that everything is running smoothly.

112
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:15,811
Yes, sir.

113
00:07:16,145 --> 00:07:19,064
Should I do everything
according to the manual?

114
00:07:29,158 --> 00:07:32,077
WE LOVE YOU, MANAGING DIRECTOR YOON
WELCOME TO FANTASY LAND

115
00:07:32,161 --> 00:07:33,328
MESSAGE FROM THE STAFF

116
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:38,959
Why would they do something
so unnecessary?

117
00:07:43,338 --> 00:07:44,840
Look over there, Mother.

118
00:07:51,847 --> 00:07:53,765
Now you say you need me.

119
00:07:53,849 --> 00:07:55,350
Do you think I'm a pushover?

120
00:07:55,434 --> 00:07:57,477
Then don't be a pushover and stay.

121
00:07:57,561 --> 00:07:58,854
I'll give you an excuse.

122
00:07:59,771 --> 00:08:01,023
Do you want a raise?

123
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:03,025
Enough with bragging about wealth.

124
00:08:03,108 --> 00:08:04,193
I don't need a raise.

125
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:07,446
But can I just hit you once?

126
00:08:11,867 --> 00:08:14,203
So I guess you were all talk.

127
00:08:14,578 --> 00:08:15,662
I knew it.

128
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:22,419
Hit me now. You won't get another chance.

129
00:08:25,088 --> 00:08:27,382
Promise me you won't demand compensation

130
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:28,675
or sue me.

131
00:08:28,759 --> 00:08:30,052
I won't.

132
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:35,724
But if you're going to hit me for real,
call the ambulance first.

133
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:38,310
Close your eyes and clench your teeth.

134
00:08:39,144 --> 00:08:40,270
Fine.

135
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:54,159
I was going to punch you,
but I flicked you instead.

136
00:08:54,243 --> 00:08:55,869
I went super easy on you.

137
00:08:58,497 --> 00:08:59,790
Let me see.

138
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:01,500
Here.

139
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,669
I thought you hit me with a rock.

140
00:09:08,632 --> 00:09:09,549
EPISODE 7

141
00:09:09,633 --> 00:09:14,012
When I came with Yi-jun,
you provided me with everything.

142
00:09:14,096 --> 00:09:17,057
This time, I had to set up my own chair.

143
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,350
She had no idea.

144
00:09:19,059 --> 00:09:22,187
Lee Hye-jung didn't expect
Kim Si-hyun to come.

145
00:09:22,271 --> 00:09:23,605
How could he have known?

146
00:09:26,191 --> 00:09:27,192
Do you think Chief Ma…

147
00:09:33,115 --> 00:09:34,908
We asked her beforehand,

148
00:09:34,992 --> 00:09:37,327
and she said
she wouldn't need an attorney.

149
00:09:37,411 --> 00:09:38,287
Is that so?

150
00:09:40,289 --> 00:09:41,915
Look, Hye-jung.

151
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:45,711
The police have the authority
to close the initial investigation.

152
00:09:46,128 --> 00:09:49,756
That means your legal response
at this stage is crucial.

153
00:09:50,841 --> 00:09:52,718
To protect your rights,

154
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:55,804
I strongly recommend
you retain an attorney.

155
00:09:59,808 --> 00:10:03,061
Why is he recommending himself
when he just appeared out of the blue?

156
00:10:03,145 --> 00:10:05,355
He just wants to show us
what he wants us to see.

157
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:07,441
This won't be easy.

158
00:10:10,319 --> 00:10:11,903
What was the last call like?

159
00:10:13,655 --> 00:10:15,282
Just a routine call to catch up.

160
00:10:17,993 --> 00:10:21,413
You received photos from Han Eun-young
right after that call, correct?

161
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:24,916
Why did you delete them?

162
00:10:27,252 --> 00:10:29,296
Did you request her to send the files?

163
00:10:31,882 --> 00:10:32,924
Answer the question.

164
00:10:39,056 --> 00:10:41,475
Deciding whether
there were elements of a crime.

165
00:10:42,059 --> 00:10:43,602
If you didn't request it, say so.

166
00:10:48,148 --> 00:10:50,525
I didn't request it.

167
00:11:04,081 --> 00:11:05,540
Secretary Han sent the files?

168
00:11:05,624 --> 00:11:07,167
It leaked from an unexpected place.

169
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,585
What about Secretary Lee?

170
00:11:09,294 --> 00:11:10,337
Staying silent.

171
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:12,506
-I'll meet her.
-It's too dangerous.

172
00:11:14,383 --> 00:11:16,927
You were the one worried
an innocent person might get hurt.

173
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:20,305
I need to know if seeing those files
will act as Ms. Lee's sword or shield.

174
00:11:20,389 --> 00:11:22,015
Only then can I prepare.

175
00:11:24,434 --> 00:11:26,728
But what on earth happened
to your forehead?

176
00:11:28,355 --> 00:11:29,981
Did a bee or a mosquito get you?

177
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:32,359
You can see it?

178
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:35,779
Let's say Han Eun-young

179
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:38,115
gave this to Lee Hye-jung.

180
00:11:38,407 --> 00:11:40,867
Why did Yoon Yi-jun
dig into this in the first place?

181
00:11:40,951 --> 00:11:42,536
As you know,

182
00:11:42,619 --> 00:11:44,704
he doesn't seem like
the type to seek justice.

183
00:11:44,788 --> 00:11:47,666
If you look closely, he does.
He's actually a decent guy.

184
00:11:48,208 --> 00:11:50,001
What? What's with you?

185
00:11:50,085 --> 00:11:51,044
Get a grip.

186
00:11:52,129 --> 00:11:55,799
What matters is,
this is putting Mr. Yoon at risk.

187
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:58,969
If that's Taekang's slush fund records,
there'll be more

188
00:11:59,052 --> 00:12:00,595
after the herbicide and chandelier.

189
00:12:00,679 --> 00:12:01,680
Mr. Yoon?

190
00:12:02,264 --> 00:12:03,932
You're being ridiculous.

191
00:12:04,224 --> 00:12:05,934
Do you think you're a real secretary?

192
00:12:06,017 --> 00:12:07,686
-I mean, Yoon Yi-jun!
-There you go.

193
00:12:11,273 --> 00:12:12,482
FANTASY LAND PR TEAM

194
00:12:17,487 --> 00:12:18,822
You said you quit on the spot.

195
00:12:19,906 --> 00:12:21,533
-Jeez.
-I thought you were too ashamed

196
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:22,701
to crawl back to him.

197
00:12:22,784 --> 00:12:25,370
How could someone like that
seem so friendly like this?

198
00:12:25,871 --> 00:12:29,124
I only went to the amusement park
because it was Jin-hyung's birthday.

199
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,250
What happened?

200
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,671
Well, the thing is…

201
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:38,175
Does it hurt a lot?

202
00:12:38,884 --> 00:12:40,552
Of all places, you had to…

203
00:12:41,678 --> 00:12:43,513
Do you know how much it hurts here?

204
00:12:44,598 --> 00:12:46,099
It's not that bad.

205
00:12:46,808 --> 00:12:48,185
It should be fine by tomorrow.

206
00:12:48,894 --> 00:12:51,229
I only put 10% of my feelings into it,

207
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:53,148
considering your public image.

208
00:12:54,191 --> 00:12:55,859
I really appreciate your generosity.

209
00:12:56,735 --> 00:12:57,736
Anyway,

210
00:12:58,487 --> 00:13:01,865
make sure you are ready
to come to work tomorrow, Special Forces.

211
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:03,241
Yes, sir.

212
00:13:05,452 --> 00:13:09,498
To celebrate resolving our labor dispute,
how about one more power trip?

213
00:13:10,165 --> 00:13:13,001
Let's take a picture here
before we go, Mother.

214
00:13:13,084 --> 00:13:14,085
Go ahead and smile.

215
00:13:15,545 --> 00:13:18,798
-There's no need for that.
-Look at you.

216
00:13:18,882 --> 00:13:20,342
You look pretty.

217
00:13:21,176 --> 00:13:22,552
-Excuse me.
-Yes, sir.

218
00:13:24,596 --> 00:13:28,225
Is this the most popular attraction
in Fantasy Land?

219
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,435
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

220
00:13:30,519 --> 00:13:31,937
It's too dark to see.

221
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:34,481
-The light should be on.
-Turn the lights on.

222
00:13:39,903 --> 00:13:41,571
-It's so beautiful.
-My goodness.

223
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:43,365
Look at the lights.

224
00:13:44,574 --> 00:13:46,409
-It's pretty.
-It's nice.

225
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,370
Would you like to ride it, sir?

226
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:49,788
I am fine…

227
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,504
But I should check if it's working.

228
00:13:59,881 --> 00:14:00,924
Should I ride it too?

229
00:14:01,007 --> 00:14:02,384
Then should I ride it alone?

230
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:03,843
I rode it a lot today.

231
00:14:07,514 --> 00:14:09,349
I'll take the picture, sir.

232
00:14:09,432 --> 00:14:11,268
One, two, three.

233
00:14:23,572 --> 00:14:25,240
But I needed an excuse to come here

234
00:14:25,824 --> 00:14:27,284
and convince you.

235
00:14:27,659 --> 00:14:30,412
He has a fiancée.
Why would he say that to me?

236
00:14:30,954 --> 00:14:33,915
As for me, I need you.

237
00:14:35,417 --> 00:14:37,085
He's just making me feel weird.

238
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:43,091
How could he hit the forehead
of Taekang's heir like this?

239
00:14:43,174 --> 00:14:44,926
-Does it hurt?
-Of course it does.

240
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:49,264
He made a mountain on your forehead.

241
00:14:49,347 --> 00:14:51,474
I can't help but respect Secretary Kang.

242
00:14:51,558 --> 00:14:53,435
He's super strong.

243
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:55,103
You sound proud of him.

244
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,439
You said you'd go back to being cold.

245
00:14:57,522 --> 00:14:58,940
It didn't work.

246
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:02,360
When I realized,
I was trying to convince him to return.

247
00:15:04,988 --> 00:15:06,615
-Can you see it?
-Clearly.

248
00:15:06,698 --> 00:15:07,532
Really?

249
00:15:07,616 --> 00:15:09,200
But will you be okay?

250
00:15:09,284 --> 00:15:11,911
Probably not. It hurts so bad.

251
00:15:11,995 --> 00:15:14,289
Jeez, not your stupid forehead.

252
00:15:14,372 --> 00:15:16,750
Chairman, shareholder meeting,
marriage, slush funds…

253
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:18,501
I can barely breathe with all this.

254
00:15:18,585 --> 00:15:20,837
Why are you complaining
about your forehead?

255
00:15:23,173 --> 00:15:24,341
Exactly.

256
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:28,720
So maybe it's okay
to have Kang Jae-hee by my side.

257
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:32,182
Of everything that's wrong in my life,

258
00:15:33,183 --> 00:15:34,976
he's the only thing that's right.

259
00:15:36,603 --> 00:15:38,605
He'll never know anyway.

260
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:39,898
You crazy punk.

261
00:15:40,398 --> 00:15:42,317
So you'll have an unrequited crush
on a guy?

262
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:44,694
You said it doesn't matter
since we're both human.

263
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:47,739
I was emphasizing unrequited love,
not it being with a guy.

264
00:15:49,366 --> 00:15:51,242
What's wrong with unrequited love?

265
00:15:51,326 --> 00:15:53,536
You say that
because you've never done it before.

266
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:56,164
Honey, I don't want to say the obvious,

267
00:15:56,247 --> 00:15:59,542
but there are things
we Homo sapiens can't hide.

268
00:16:00,585 --> 00:16:03,880
One of them is unrequited love,
what you insist on doing.

269
00:16:04,506 --> 00:16:06,257
It will show no matter what you do,

270
00:16:06,758 --> 00:16:08,927
like your stupid forehead. Okay?

271
00:16:15,934 --> 00:16:17,102
Gosh, what's wrong?

272
00:16:23,692 --> 00:16:25,110
I'm sorry.

273
00:16:25,193 --> 00:16:28,571
The bus has broken down,
so please take another bus.

274
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:33,159
I'm sorry, everyone.

275
00:16:33,243 --> 00:16:34,327
Hello, sir.

276
00:16:35,495 --> 00:16:36,621
Why aren't you here yet?

277
00:16:36,705 --> 00:16:38,164
What did you say?

278
00:16:38,707 --> 00:16:40,291
Was there an accident? Are you hurt?

279
00:16:40,375 --> 00:16:41,918
Are you severely, badly injured?

280
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,169
I could send a helicopter.

281
00:16:45,714 --> 00:16:46,965
The bus just broke down?

282
00:16:47,924 --> 00:16:48,883
Okay.

283
00:16:49,676 --> 00:16:53,096
Don't think about rushing here.
Just be careful, okay?

284
00:16:56,683 --> 00:16:57,726
"Be careful"?

285
00:17:04,274 --> 00:17:05,483
Mr. Yoon.

286
00:17:06,735 --> 00:17:07,736
I'm sorry I'm late.

287
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:10,780
The bus suddenly stopped on the road.

288
00:17:11,281 --> 00:17:12,449
I had to run here.

289
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:16,202
Can I drink some water?

290
00:17:22,292 --> 00:17:23,334
Here.

291
00:17:25,003 --> 00:17:26,045
Thank you.

292
00:17:27,547 --> 00:17:29,966
Call first if something happens.
Don't make me worry.

293
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:34,512
What's with you?

294
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:37,724
Drink up.

295
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:40,685
No, it's fine.

296
00:17:40,769 --> 00:17:42,687
It's yours. I can't possibly drink it.

297
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:45,815
Don't you want to drink it
because it's mine

298
00:17:46,232 --> 00:17:47,942
or because it's bitter?

299
00:17:49,611 --> 00:17:52,155
You're such a baby.
It's good for you, so drink it.

300
00:17:53,156 --> 00:17:54,991
-Now.
-Yes, sir.

301
00:17:56,785 --> 00:17:57,744
Thank you.

302
00:18:07,587 --> 00:18:08,588
It's so bitter.

303
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:16,513
Why did you chuckle?

304
00:18:16,596 --> 00:18:18,640
I was in great agony just now.

305
00:18:19,307 --> 00:18:21,226
-Don't laugh.
-I laughed because you're cute.

306
00:18:21,309 --> 00:18:23,353
Don't say things like that.

307
00:18:23,895 --> 00:18:25,355
But you are cute.

308
00:18:28,191 --> 00:18:29,984
You think it doesn't sound manly?

309
00:18:30,068 --> 00:18:33,071
You want me to say
"you're cool" instead of "cute"?

310
00:18:33,154 --> 00:18:35,406
No, it's not like that, but…

311
00:18:36,366 --> 00:18:38,785
-Anyway, don't say it.
-I'll do whatever I want.

312
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:42,580
I'm saying you're cute because you are.
I don't need your permission.

313
00:18:42,664 --> 00:18:44,457
Stop bullying me!

314
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:47,961
Good morning.

315
00:18:51,297 --> 00:18:52,131
What?

316
00:18:55,385 --> 00:18:56,386
What's going on?

317
00:18:56,803 --> 00:19:00,640
Taekang Goddess Lee Hye-jung
and Taekang Idol Kim Si-hyun

318
00:19:00,723 --> 00:19:03,476
were not romantically involved at first.

319
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:06,563
But Taespatch caught them openly dating,

320
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:09,107
going back and forth
between each other's homes.

321
00:19:09,190 --> 00:19:10,608
Anyway, long story short,

322
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:13,820
they're no longer coworkers.

323
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:16,030
They're lovers.

324
00:19:16,114 --> 00:19:17,991
Attorney Kim, what's your official stance?

325
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:19,534
Is this story true?

326
00:19:20,493 --> 00:19:21,870
Half of it is.

327
00:19:21,953 --> 00:19:24,706
-Keeping it vague like a true lawyer.
-Is it a yes or a no?

328
00:19:24,789 --> 00:19:26,875
It's true that we went on a date,

329
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:29,294
but I got dumped.

330
00:19:29,377 --> 00:19:30,879
That's too bad.

331
00:19:30,962 --> 00:19:33,339
Welcome to the LRA, Mr. Kim Si-hyun.

332
00:19:34,132 --> 00:19:35,884
Do not hesitate to join us.

333
00:19:37,802 --> 00:19:39,137
Wait.

334
00:19:39,888 --> 00:19:43,016
But I still went on a date
before getting dumped,

335
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:44,517
so what will my status be?

336
00:19:44,601 --> 00:19:46,185
People who went on dates…

337
00:19:46,269 --> 00:19:47,478
Let me know later.

338
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:51,065
Anyway, welcome.

339
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:55,737
Ms. L dumped Mr. K?

340
00:19:56,154 --> 00:19:57,530
Attorney Kim admitted it.

341
00:19:59,741 --> 00:20:01,034
Here comes Mr. K.

342
00:20:02,911 --> 00:20:04,120
I'll go ahead first.

343
00:20:15,590 --> 00:20:17,508
I'm not here to chat
about our relationship.

344
00:20:19,177 --> 00:20:21,137
Would you be willing
to meet Mr. Yoon Yi-jun?

345
00:20:21,888 --> 00:20:24,057
I had to stop him
from getting involved for now.

346
00:20:24,974 --> 00:20:27,018
I'm not forcing you. Do as you please.

347
00:20:28,019 --> 00:20:28,937
Why?

348
00:20:31,189 --> 00:20:33,316
You're a client. I'm your attorney.

349
00:20:33,399 --> 00:20:34,943
I'm just doing my job.

350
00:20:39,280 --> 00:20:41,407
How did you know
I was at the police station?

351
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:43,117
The police called me.

352
00:20:44,619 --> 00:20:45,745
You're all in on this.

353
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,795
Calling us all in on it
is a little insulting.

354
00:20:54,921 --> 00:20:57,715
I'm the type who seeks justice.

355
00:20:58,675 --> 00:21:00,885
You know better than anyone

356
00:21:01,678 --> 00:21:03,262
that this isn't the time to argue.

357
00:21:03,846 --> 00:21:06,432
You think I'm the only one
who got a call from the police?

358
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:10,687
Whoever made Secretary Han like that
must've gotten one too.

359
00:21:11,396 --> 00:21:14,148
If they're closer to the police,

360
00:21:14,232 --> 00:21:15,817
they'll have more intel.

361
00:21:17,193 --> 00:21:19,112
Your cards have been revealed.

362
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:20,905
If you're not going to tell the police,

363
00:21:20,989 --> 00:21:24,325
at least tell your attorney, okay?

364
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:27,912
Don't think of stabbing me
in the back again.

365
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:33,543
Did you try to stab me?

366
00:21:35,336 --> 00:21:37,755
I'm too anxious to sit in front of you.

367
00:21:39,257 --> 00:21:41,300
I'm only sitting next to you from now on.

368
00:21:45,013 --> 00:21:47,515
THE ELEVATOR EXCLUSIVELY FOR EXECUTIVES
IS UNDER REPAIR

369
00:21:47,598 --> 00:21:49,517
PLEASE USE THE ELEVATOR FOR EMPLOYEES

370
00:22:04,282 --> 00:22:06,159
Don't overreact and just come closer.

371
00:22:34,020 --> 00:22:35,563
They have a thing.

372
00:22:36,397 --> 00:22:38,399
The flower shop
and the chicken joint owner?

373
00:22:38,483 --> 00:22:40,651
It's the most unlikely pair
in the neighborhood.

374
00:22:40,735 --> 00:22:41,986
Enemies and lovers!

375
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:44,697
Just one little twist,
and they're falling for each other.

376
00:22:44,781 --> 00:22:47,867
They say affection,
even grudging affection, can't be stopped.

377
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:49,494
They fell in love through fighting.

378
00:22:49,577 --> 00:22:51,329
I'm sure you have no grudging affection.

379
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:54,165
-Why not?
-Your husband is handsome.

380
00:23:21,150 --> 00:23:24,237
I'd develop affection
if my husband had a face like his.

381
00:23:25,404 --> 00:23:27,240
That was a long time ago.

382
00:23:27,323 --> 00:23:28,825
He's just an old man now.

383
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:31,369
Do you still do live streaming
with a mask on?

384
00:23:32,078 --> 00:23:33,704
Do you make money through it?

385
00:23:33,788 --> 00:23:36,332
With your help, I can make money.

386
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:39,127
So please like and subscribe.

387
00:23:39,752 --> 00:23:40,920
I love you.

388
00:23:42,088 --> 00:23:44,841
Okay, I'll like, subscribe,
and hit the notification button.

389
00:23:46,217 --> 00:23:48,136
You're picking teeth after drinking water?

390
00:23:49,887 --> 00:23:51,347
A job satisfaction survey?

391
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:54,851
Yes. I'm busy preparing for an event,
so you'll be doing it first.

392
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:56,519
-So go ahead.
-Okay.

393
00:23:57,311 --> 00:23:59,147
But are you sure I can't help?

394
00:23:59,564 --> 00:24:00,982
You've worked overtime for days.

395
00:24:01,065 --> 00:24:05,111
You have prepared
such a boring speech for me.

396
00:24:06,696 --> 00:24:07,655
Secretary Kwon.

397
00:24:09,031 --> 00:24:10,074
Give me the next one.

398
00:24:14,745 --> 00:24:16,414
What are you doing? Aren't you going?

399
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:18,958
I'm leaving. I'll be back, sir.

400
00:24:21,669 --> 00:24:23,671
Don't give him any work
for the time being.

401
00:24:23,754 --> 00:24:25,131
I have a personal task for him.

402
00:24:25,214 --> 00:24:27,049
I must've been Cinderella in my past life.

403
00:24:27,884 --> 00:24:31,304
-The stepmother dotes on the stepsister.
-Do you want me

404
00:24:31,846 --> 00:24:33,723
to show you how I dote on someone?

405
00:24:34,765 --> 00:24:37,602
Do you really want to see
what a stepmother can do?

406
00:24:40,730 --> 00:24:43,107
JOB SATISFACTION SURVEY
KANG JAE-HEE

407
00:24:46,485 --> 00:24:47,987
BENEFITS AND CORPORATE CULTURE

408
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,614
How do you deal with stress?

409
00:24:49,697 --> 00:24:50,740
I like to be physical.

410
00:24:50,823 --> 00:24:52,783
I do taekwondo and jujitsu.

411
00:24:52,867 --> 00:24:55,036
I've been boxing these days as well.

412
00:24:55,119 --> 00:24:59,457
But if I can't find the time to exercise,
I go for a run

413
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:00,541
by the Han River.

414
00:25:01,083 --> 00:25:03,794
I compete with the cruise
when I'm running at night.

415
00:25:03,878 --> 00:25:05,838
You know that race

416
00:25:05,922 --> 00:25:08,549
between a person and a subway on TV?

417
00:25:08,633 --> 00:25:11,552
I love to challenge myself like that.

418
00:25:13,763 --> 00:25:15,765
RELATIONSHIP WITH BOSS AND COLLEAGUES

419
00:25:15,848 --> 00:25:18,434
SATISFACTION WITH BOSS

420
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:23,064
This survey

421
00:25:24,523 --> 00:25:27,443
is anonymous for sure, right?

422
00:25:30,154 --> 00:25:31,155
Recently,

423
00:25:32,573 --> 00:25:35,618
my boss has been a little bit weird.

424
00:25:40,998 --> 00:25:42,792
His facial expression…

425
00:25:44,377 --> 00:25:45,753
Don't make me worry.

426
00:25:46,170 --> 00:25:48,631
And his tone and behavior.

427
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:51,592
His face is weird too.

428
00:25:53,344 --> 00:25:54,929
But what's weirder is

429
00:25:55,012 --> 00:25:57,431
that friend of yours
whose identity you can't reveal?

430
00:25:58,599 --> 00:26:00,810
Whenever they see their boss act funny,

431
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:03,312
they feel a bit confused

432
00:26:03,896 --> 00:26:06,148
-and funny.
-Exactly.

433
00:26:06,524 --> 00:26:07,650
Is the boss handsome?

434
00:26:09,068 --> 00:26:11,320
-Well, a little.
-Does he have money?

435
00:26:11,862 --> 00:26:13,281
He's definitely not poor.

436
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,075
That's it.

437
00:26:16,617 --> 00:26:19,370
Why rack your brain
over such a simple problem?

438
00:26:21,122 --> 00:26:23,749
Your secretary friend
whose identity you can't reveal

439
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,376
and the boss

440
00:26:26,335 --> 00:26:28,462
-are currently…
-Currently?

441
00:26:29,505 --> 00:26:32,300
waiting for the right time to quit.
It's a game of chicken.

442
00:26:32,383 --> 00:26:33,676
They both want to quit.

443
00:26:33,759 --> 00:26:36,470
Their hearts must be all over the place.

444
00:26:37,305 --> 00:26:39,640
-Take this and go home.
-What?

445
00:26:39,724 --> 00:26:42,101
Just go home! You're not helping.

446
00:26:42,935 --> 00:26:45,646
Anyway, your secretary friend

447
00:26:46,314 --> 00:26:47,898
should just ask the boss.

448
00:26:55,239 --> 00:26:57,241
They don't even understand
their own feelings.

449
00:26:57,325 --> 00:27:00,369
How can they figure out someone else's?

450
00:27:00,453 --> 00:27:02,455
You're a frustrating one.

451
00:27:08,544 --> 00:27:10,713
MR. YOON

452
00:27:12,923 --> 00:27:13,841
Yes, sir.

453
00:27:13,924 --> 00:27:15,051
Where are you?

454
00:27:15,968 --> 00:27:18,346
Every single time, how are you so…

455
00:27:18,888 --> 00:27:21,015
The job satisfaction survey
you did today--

456
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:24,101
Forget it.

457
00:27:24,560 --> 00:27:27,188
I'll give you ten minutes
to come over here.

458
00:27:27,271 --> 00:27:28,564
Move it!

459
00:27:32,526 --> 00:27:33,527
SATISFACTION WITH BOSS

460
00:27:33,611 --> 00:27:34,779
He didn't even

461
00:27:35,529 --> 00:27:36,822
circle a number.

462
00:27:38,491 --> 00:27:41,035
He thinks I'm worth zero points.

463
00:27:52,463 --> 00:27:54,465
-This way.
-Thank you.

464
00:27:58,302 --> 00:27:59,303
Sir.

465
00:28:00,930 --> 00:28:04,558
I told you I'd go to your place.
Why did you want to meet here?

466
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:14,110
I happened to have business here.

467
00:28:17,071 --> 00:28:18,072
Also,

468
00:28:20,157 --> 00:28:21,325
they sell flowers here.

469
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,202
They sell flowers here?

470
00:28:24,078 --> 00:28:26,330
-Here.
-It's for me?

471
00:28:31,001 --> 00:28:32,002
Have a seat.

472
00:28:38,968 --> 00:28:40,136
WE SELL FLOWERS

473
00:28:40,219 --> 00:28:41,637
They really sell flowers.

474
00:28:46,142 --> 00:28:49,228
All right. Order whatever you want.

475
00:28:49,437 --> 00:28:50,396
Whatever I want?

476
00:28:51,647 --> 00:28:53,441
I can buy you the whole bar.

477
00:28:53,524 --> 00:28:56,485
No, I can even buy you the whole building.

478
00:28:57,111 --> 00:28:58,904
Why are you doing this all of a sudden?

479
00:28:58,988 --> 00:29:00,364
That's the kind of boss I am.

480
00:29:00,865 --> 00:29:03,284
A perfect boss
with talent and money to spare.

481
00:29:03,826 --> 00:29:05,744
I'm a five-out-of-five boss.

482
00:29:13,502 --> 00:29:15,671
What's with you these days?

483
00:29:16,630 --> 00:29:19,049
-What?
-Why are you being nice to me?

484
00:29:20,801 --> 00:29:22,470
-I am?
-Yes.

485
00:29:23,637 --> 00:29:26,515
Speaking of which, by any chance,

486
00:29:30,978 --> 00:29:32,354
do you like me?

487
00:29:51,999 --> 00:29:54,376
Can I see you for a moment?

488
00:29:55,336 --> 00:29:57,671
Where are you? I'll come to you.

489
00:30:09,350 --> 00:30:10,809
You're going home late.

490
00:30:10,893 --> 00:30:13,187
Why are you still here?

491
00:30:14,104 --> 00:30:15,105
I was working late.

492
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,567
Why did you ask
if you're not going to believe me,

493
00:30:18,651 --> 00:30:19,944
pretending to know nothing?

494
00:30:22,655 --> 00:30:24,114
Why are you going back and forth?

495
00:30:24,198 --> 00:30:26,325
Because you're going back and forth.

496
00:30:27,201 --> 00:30:28,410
I hold grudges, you know.

497
00:30:29,245 --> 00:30:31,830
I've been thinking it over
ever since I got rejected.

498
00:30:31,914 --> 00:30:33,415
So I see it now.

499
00:30:34,542 --> 00:30:36,794
You said my question
about why you approached me

500
00:30:37,753 --> 00:30:39,004
was the answer in itself.

501
00:30:39,672 --> 00:30:42,800
If I had harmed Secretary Han,
I wouldn't have asked such a question.

502
00:30:44,176 --> 00:30:47,763
Yet I naively questioned you back.

503
00:30:49,390 --> 00:30:52,309
You were testing whether I was bad,
realized I wasn't,

504
00:30:52,393 --> 00:30:53,811
felt guilty, and dumped me.

505
00:30:54,687 --> 00:30:56,772
You know why Secretary Han died,

506
00:30:56,855 --> 00:30:58,857
but you don't know who did it.

507
00:30:59,525 --> 00:31:02,069
And you're too scared
to trust anyone too easily.

508
00:31:05,489 --> 00:31:06,657
Don't be scared.

509
00:31:07,449 --> 00:31:09,994
I'll be your lawyer, your ex,

510
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:13,539
whatever you need. So don't be scared.

511
00:31:31,473 --> 00:31:32,641
Do you understand

512
00:31:34,184 --> 00:31:36,645
what you are even asking?

513
00:31:37,021 --> 00:31:37,855
I do.

514
00:31:40,608 --> 00:31:42,985
You hate most things

515
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:44,987
and rarely like anything.

516
00:31:46,614 --> 00:31:50,034
And when you like something,
you really make it obvious,

517
00:31:52,369 --> 00:31:55,289
like your cat and your action figures.

518
00:31:56,332 --> 00:32:00,794
I'm just wondering if I'm at their level.

519
00:32:03,714 --> 00:32:04,715
Fair enough.

520
00:32:06,216 --> 00:32:08,093
That would be
the most plausible conclusion

521
00:32:08,177 --> 00:32:09,678
you would come to.

522
00:32:11,430 --> 00:32:14,600
You are definitely not at their level.

523
00:32:15,684 --> 00:32:17,227
I see.

524
00:32:17,895 --> 00:32:19,521
I got butterflies for nothing.

525
00:32:22,733 --> 00:32:24,610
Excuse me. I have to take this call.

526
00:32:40,876 --> 00:32:41,877
You…

527
00:32:43,045 --> 00:32:45,297
are way above that level.

528
00:32:48,258 --> 00:32:50,844
That's why I want to keep you
by my side for a long time.

529
00:32:51,345 --> 00:32:52,304
Okay.

530
00:32:55,891 --> 00:32:58,602
Sir, I think you should check your phone.

531
00:33:02,231 --> 00:33:04,525
MISSED CALLS
NOISY KIM

532
00:33:35,639 --> 00:33:39,351
I can leave if you feel uncomfortable.

533
00:33:52,322 --> 00:33:54,450
I guess coming here with you at this hour

534
00:33:55,159 --> 00:33:56,326
shows a level of trust.

535
00:34:03,834 --> 00:34:06,920
Unfortunately, I don't trust you yet.

536
00:34:08,255 --> 00:34:10,299
You were laying low to protect yourself.

537
00:34:11,175 --> 00:34:13,802
At least, that is
what Attorney Kim assumes.

538
00:34:13,886 --> 00:34:15,429
I feel the same.

539
00:34:16,638 --> 00:34:20,684
You should be grateful
that Attorney Kim is your friend.

540
00:34:35,115 --> 00:34:36,366
It has a recording function.

541
00:34:38,911 --> 00:34:42,206
I gifted it to Secretary Han,
who was my first junior colleague.

542
00:34:44,666 --> 00:34:48,754
A secretary has to execute
their boss's every word to perfection.

543
00:34:49,505 --> 00:34:53,425
In that sense,
you are notorious for being demanding.

544
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:55,636
As such, Secretary Han

545
00:34:56,386 --> 00:34:58,096
carried this around like a talisman.

546
00:34:59,556 --> 00:35:01,767
Why do you have it
when it was a gift to her?

547
00:35:03,519 --> 00:35:06,939
Do you think I replaced
Secretary Han's desk because I was bored?

548
00:35:07,022 --> 00:35:08,565
Weren't you looking for the phone?

549
00:35:10,067 --> 00:35:11,235
I had no idea about that.

550
00:35:12,778 --> 00:35:15,489
I just thought she used an unknown number
out of anxiety.

551
00:35:17,407 --> 00:35:20,410
Where did they find that phone?

552
00:35:24,665 --> 00:35:25,666
So this pen contains

553
00:35:26,416 --> 00:35:29,503
information that would make me trust you?

554
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:35,759
I have a condition.

555
00:35:39,429 --> 00:35:41,139
Share everything with me.

556
00:35:41,515 --> 00:35:44,518
Whatever you, Attorney Kim,
and Park Min-hwan from Accounting Team 3

557
00:35:44,601 --> 00:35:46,019
have been preparing.

558
00:35:46,103 --> 00:35:48,730
I won't let you. You'll be in danger.

559
00:35:49,273 --> 00:35:51,066
As you all know,

560
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:53,360
a lot gets discussed
in the chairman's office.

561
00:35:54,695 --> 00:35:58,907
I'll share as much as I can
without risking my dignity as a secretary.

562
00:36:00,576 --> 00:36:01,869
You'd better be prepared.

563
00:36:02,744 --> 00:36:04,246
It could get really dangerous.

564
00:36:04,997 --> 00:36:07,583
If I put you in danger,

565
00:36:10,627 --> 00:36:12,713
I don't think he'll let me off.

566
00:36:12,796 --> 00:36:15,257
Unfortunately, I don't think
I can help you with that.

567
00:36:16,258 --> 00:36:17,759
I already have enough problems.

568
00:36:30,814 --> 00:36:34,443
Are you being threatened or followed?

569
00:36:39,114 --> 00:36:40,908
He wears the same shoes every time

570
00:36:41,867 --> 00:36:43,994
and stands under the light
outside my apartment.

571
00:36:47,915 --> 00:36:50,417
I think he was checking to see
how much I knew.

572
00:36:55,714 --> 00:36:57,883
TAKE CARE OF LEE HYE-JUNG FIRST

573
00:37:04,473 --> 00:37:08,518
It felt like a threat that
I'd end up like Secretary Han if I talked.

574
00:37:09,186 --> 00:37:11,563
If the police didn't find me
on that phone,

575
00:37:12,105 --> 00:37:13,815
that threat would've still worked.

576
00:37:16,193 --> 00:37:18,737
I'll check if he's the same man
chasing Park Min-hwan.

577
00:37:18,820 --> 00:37:20,489
The man who's after Park Min-hwan.

578
00:37:20,989 --> 00:37:22,449
The one who killed Han Eun-young.

579
00:37:23,825 --> 00:37:25,202
The one wearing the same shoes.

580
00:37:27,245 --> 00:37:28,622
That could all be the same guy.

581
00:37:28,705 --> 00:37:30,123
What do we do with Lee Hye-jung?

582
00:37:30,207 --> 00:37:32,960
Shouldn't we be protecting her
instead of questioning her?

583
00:37:37,756 --> 00:37:40,092
KIM SI-HYUN

584
00:37:40,175 --> 00:37:41,343
LEE HYE-JUNG

585
00:37:48,392 --> 00:37:49,476
YOON NA-JUNG

586
00:37:50,519 --> 00:37:53,939
You and I will tail Lee Hye-jung
until the second questioning.

587
00:37:54,231 --> 00:37:55,232
Yes, sir.

588
00:37:55,983 --> 00:37:58,860
So, Jae-hee did one thing right this time.

589
00:37:59,486 --> 00:38:01,279
Yoon Yi-jun probably has no idea

590
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:03,490
who Jae-hee really is.

591
00:38:05,492 --> 00:38:08,495
On the other hand,
Detective Kang knows Yoon Yi-jun well.

592
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:15,127
That's what worries me.
The more you know, the more you'll lean

593
00:38:18,547 --> 00:38:19,673
one way or the other.

594
00:38:25,804 --> 00:38:28,807
I jog here
whenever I have a lot on my mind.

595
00:38:29,891 --> 00:38:31,810
Would you like to jog as well?

596
00:38:31,893 --> 00:38:32,853
No.

597
00:38:36,148 --> 00:38:38,567
Don't worry about Secretary Lee.

598
00:38:40,277 --> 00:38:42,154
You assigned her security,

599
00:38:42,237 --> 00:38:44,031
and there's Attorney Kim as well.

600
00:38:44,114 --> 00:38:45,407
Plus, the police

601
00:38:47,034 --> 00:38:48,952
will still keep an eye on the situation.

602
00:38:54,124 --> 00:38:55,459
Do you regret doing this?

603
00:38:57,252 --> 00:38:58,378
Sometimes.

604
00:38:59,629 --> 00:39:00,756
It's clear that

605
00:39:00,839 --> 00:39:03,842
the slush fund won't be used
for anything good.

606
00:39:03,925 --> 00:39:05,719
That's the kind of place Taekang is.

607
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:07,846
Bad intentions

608
00:39:09,431 --> 00:39:10,724
justify their actions.

609
00:39:12,184 --> 00:39:14,478
Those who are unrelated
to those bad intentions

610
00:39:14,978 --> 00:39:16,855
can waver and get hurt.

611
00:39:20,400 --> 00:39:22,110
That's why I'm digging.

612
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,406
I was naive.

613
00:39:30,202 --> 00:39:31,411
I acted too rashly.

614
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:39,628
What if I just swept it under the rug

615
00:39:41,838 --> 00:39:43,548
when I first found out?

616
00:39:45,175 --> 00:39:47,552
Would things have gone this far?

617
00:40:00,273 --> 00:40:02,859
Do you know why I left the military?

618
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:11,118
No footprints below the ridge.

619
00:40:11,660 --> 00:40:12,994
Roger. Into the forest.

620
00:40:14,329 --> 00:40:17,958
I learned that life is a journey you take
with someone you can trust.

621
00:40:20,168 --> 00:40:23,547
Sergeant Go was
that kind of senior and comrade to me.

622
00:40:24,381 --> 00:40:26,550
When Jin-hyung was just over 100 days old,

623
00:40:27,008 --> 00:40:29,052
we were sent on a hostage rescue mission.

624
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:58,290
Have mercy on me.

625
00:41:00,125 --> 00:41:01,126
Kang Jae-hee.

626
00:41:10,927 --> 00:41:12,762
Shots fired. Find out what happened.

627
00:41:15,182 --> 00:41:16,016
Sergeant Go!

628
00:41:18,268 --> 00:41:19,394
Staff Sergeant Kang.

629
00:41:19,895 --> 00:41:22,063
It's a relief you're alive.

630
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:29,070
No!

631
00:41:29,154 --> 00:41:30,363
Sergeant Go!

632
00:41:30,447 --> 00:41:32,657
No!

633
00:41:32,741 --> 00:41:34,242
Sergeant Go!

634
00:41:34,910 --> 00:41:36,536
Sergeant Go!

635
00:41:37,245 --> 00:41:38,538
Sergeant Go.

636
00:41:40,165 --> 00:41:41,875
No!

637
00:41:42,751 --> 00:41:44,085
During the mission,

638
00:41:44,920 --> 00:41:47,297
because of my moment's hesitation,

639
00:41:48,340 --> 00:41:49,257
Sergeant Go died.

640
00:41:50,300 --> 00:41:52,469
There was nothing I could do.

641
00:41:54,721 --> 00:41:56,806
I've had
the same dream thousands of times.

642
00:41:58,099 --> 00:41:59,392
7TH SPECIAL MISSION UNIT

643
00:41:59,476 --> 00:42:01,311
But even in my dreams,

644
00:42:02,812 --> 00:42:04,522
I could never save Sergeant Go.

645
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:11,738
That's why I ran away.

646
00:42:16,284 --> 00:42:17,869
But I regret it a little bit.

647
00:42:20,956 --> 00:42:23,458
I shouldn't have run away like that.

648
00:42:29,547 --> 00:42:31,925
After years of wandering,

649
00:42:32,342 --> 00:42:34,010
I finally promised Sergeant Go

650
00:42:34,427 --> 00:42:37,639
I'd make Jin-hyung's world a little safer.

651
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:46,690
Don't run away, Mr. Yoon.

652
00:42:47,816 --> 00:42:49,442
You already know what to do.

653
00:42:50,068 --> 00:42:53,238
The fact that you know
what you can do means

654
00:42:53,738 --> 00:42:55,573
you're heading in the right direction.

655
00:43:05,542 --> 00:43:06,793
Special Forces.

656
00:43:07,919 --> 00:43:09,796
Are you comforting me?

657
00:43:13,216 --> 00:43:15,427
I felt like I wouldn't have
the chance later.

658
00:43:16,886 --> 00:43:18,513
You never know what will happen.

659
00:43:19,306 --> 00:43:20,473
Well,

660
00:43:22,475 --> 00:43:23,893
you did comfort me.

661
00:43:26,313 --> 00:43:27,814
We might become sworn enemies,

662
00:43:29,524 --> 00:43:31,735
and you might end up hating me.

663
00:43:46,666 --> 00:43:47,917
I doubt it.

664
00:44:03,183 --> 00:44:04,184
When we first met,

665
00:44:07,270 --> 00:44:08,605
do you remember what I said?

666
00:44:09,564 --> 00:44:12,400
Remember I said I would've fallen for you
if you were a girl?

667
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,781
If I really were a girl,

668
00:44:19,949 --> 00:44:21,242
would you have fallen for me?

669
00:44:23,411 --> 00:44:24,245
No.

670
00:44:31,878 --> 00:44:33,380
What's the point?

671
00:44:34,589 --> 00:44:37,217
Why even entertain pointless what-ifs
about being a girl?

672
00:44:39,344 --> 00:44:40,428
You are…

673
00:44:42,222 --> 00:44:43,431
just you.

674
00:44:46,518 --> 00:44:47,519
Right.

675
00:44:49,270 --> 00:44:51,940
It was a pointless what-if.

676
00:45:18,216 --> 00:45:20,301
What kind of a situation is this?

677
00:45:33,106 --> 00:45:35,525
Isn't it obvious?

678
00:45:36,818 --> 00:45:39,279
I'm trying to buy my secretary a suit.

679
00:45:39,362 --> 00:45:40,905
Why do I need your permission?

680
00:45:40,989 --> 00:45:42,740
Because I am that secretary.

681
00:45:43,324 --> 00:45:45,660
I'll dress up properly for the event.

682
00:45:45,743 --> 00:45:46,995
I doubt it.

683
00:45:47,662 --> 00:45:50,457
This is a very important event.

684
00:45:50,540 --> 00:45:52,959
I make the opening remarks
and receive an award.

685
00:45:53,376 --> 00:45:55,086
I'll be in a lot of photos as well.

686
00:45:55,462 --> 00:45:58,465
If the secretary who serves me
looks like a mess,

687
00:45:58,548 --> 00:46:00,508
what do you think will happen to my image?

688
00:46:05,472 --> 00:46:07,932
He'll find out if I get measured.

689
00:46:08,349 --> 00:46:09,642
This is part of your job.

690
00:46:09,726 --> 00:46:11,853
Get measured while I'm still being nice.

691
00:46:11,936 --> 00:46:15,315
The thing is
that this makes me uncomfortable.

692
00:46:20,445 --> 00:46:21,529
Why are you refusing?

693
00:46:22,697 --> 00:46:25,825
Other people couldn't wear this suit
even if they wanted to.

694
00:46:28,453 --> 00:46:29,412
Is it too much?

695
00:46:31,789 --> 00:46:32,957
Well,

696
00:46:33,791 --> 00:46:35,960
it's not a good excuse to make
to a rich man.

697
00:46:38,505 --> 00:46:39,631
Or…

698
00:46:43,134 --> 00:46:45,345
is there another reason
why you can't be measured?

699
00:46:57,357 --> 00:46:59,067
I'll get measured.

700
00:47:02,111 --> 00:47:03,279
Please turn around.

701
00:47:10,203 --> 00:47:12,121
Are you going to stay here, Ms. Lee?

702
00:47:12,580 --> 00:47:13,414
Yes.

703
00:47:14,165 --> 00:47:16,543
-You make me uncomfortable.
-I'm not.

704
00:47:16,626 --> 00:47:18,127
But I am.

705
00:47:18,211 --> 00:47:20,004
Is keeping a distance a habit of yours?

706
00:47:20,755 --> 00:47:23,925
You're probably the only person
to ask a boss to leave the room

707
00:47:24,592 --> 00:47:26,261
because you're uncomfortable.

708
00:47:29,639 --> 00:47:30,765
He feels uncomfortable.

709
00:47:31,683 --> 00:47:32,684
Let's leave.

710
00:47:47,407 --> 00:47:48,575
Your guess is correct.

711
00:47:49,367 --> 00:47:51,077
If you want to tell Mr. Yoon, go ahead.

712
00:47:51,160 --> 00:47:54,914
However, if something happens to him,

713
00:47:54,998 --> 00:47:56,666
you'll have to take responsibility.

714
00:47:57,166 --> 00:47:58,835
Are you threatening me?

715
00:47:59,669 --> 00:48:00,837
I'm asking you a favor.

716
00:48:01,379 --> 00:48:03,798
I can't reveal the truth
due to the nature of my work,

717
00:48:03,881 --> 00:48:06,050
but after things have been sorted out,

718
00:48:06,884 --> 00:48:08,636
I'll tell him myself.

719
00:48:34,120 --> 00:48:37,040
Something's up, so we can't do it
before the shareholder meeting.

720
00:48:38,166 --> 00:48:40,460
Can we postpone the wedding?

721
00:48:41,252 --> 00:48:42,712
I think you need to elaborate.

722
00:48:43,421 --> 00:48:46,007
Like the reason why
and what the issue is about.

723
00:48:46,090 --> 00:48:48,384
I didn't know you'd be interested.

724
00:48:48,468 --> 00:48:49,969
I'm not.

725
00:48:52,764 --> 00:48:54,432
So I don't need an explanation.

726
00:48:54,515 --> 00:48:56,643
But I don't intend to postpone it.

727
00:48:58,269 --> 00:49:00,980
If you can't postpone it,
move it up instead.

728
00:49:01,773 --> 00:49:02,649
Shall we do it now?

729
00:49:03,399 --> 00:49:04,359
I'm not sure.

730
00:49:04,901 --> 00:49:08,655
I'm a little too interested
in your love life to do anything now.

731
00:49:19,207 --> 00:49:23,169
So let's get married
when I'm at my most beautiful.

732
00:49:26,089 --> 00:49:27,298
I love you too.

733
00:49:34,138 --> 00:49:35,098
What are you doing?

734
00:49:35,181 --> 00:49:36,974
Hey, did you finish measuring?

735
00:49:57,203 --> 00:49:58,413
I'll go home now.

736
00:50:00,957 --> 00:50:02,875
Fine. I'll explain first.

737
00:50:03,710 --> 00:50:06,504
You know I don't allow
any room for misunderstanding.

738
00:50:06,587 --> 00:50:10,508
About "I love you too."
The particle "too" implies

739
00:50:10,591 --> 00:50:12,385
you're adding to something said before.

740
00:50:12,468 --> 00:50:14,095
But I swear that I never--

741
00:50:14,178 --> 00:50:16,556
I'm sorry I barged in.

742
00:50:17,890 --> 00:50:18,766
I apologize.

743
00:50:21,519 --> 00:50:23,855
Listen. The point I'm trying to make is…

744
00:50:37,910 --> 00:50:39,787
-Hello.
-Hello.

745
00:50:39,871 --> 00:50:41,205
-Welcome.
-Hello.

746
00:50:41,998 --> 00:50:43,666
-Hello.
-Please look this way.

747
00:50:43,750 --> 00:50:45,209
-Hello.
-Hi.

748
00:50:45,293 --> 00:50:46,919
-Hello.
-Hello.

749
00:50:47,754 --> 00:50:49,213
-Hi.
-Hello.

750
00:50:49,297 --> 00:50:50,381
Please look this way.

751
00:50:50,465 --> 00:50:53,301
-Over this way!
-Hello.

752
00:50:53,384 --> 00:50:54,719
Sir, over here.

753
00:50:54,802 --> 00:50:56,596
-Please look this way.
-Like him or not,

754
00:50:56,679 --> 00:50:58,222
he's clearly the best-looking here.

755
00:50:58,890 --> 00:51:00,767
Please say a word, sir.

756
00:51:02,268 --> 00:51:03,728
You look decent, Secretary Kang.

757
00:51:03,811 --> 00:51:06,355
I wonder why you got the suit
when I did all the work.

758
00:51:19,619 --> 00:51:20,495
He's here.

759
00:51:26,626 --> 00:51:29,587
If you ditch your wife and cheat,
you go to hell.

760
00:51:31,339 --> 00:51:32,173
Smile.

761
00:51:36,719 --> 00:51:39,180
You'll go to that hell first then.

762
00:51:41,098 --> 00:51:42,892
Why are you being so grumpy?

763
00:51:43,935 --> 00:51:45,978
Is Secretary Kang not treating you well?

764
00:52:02,578 --> 00:52:03,788
SEOK-JIN

765
00:52:07,124 --> 00:52:09,669
The number you've dialed is unavailable.

766
00:52:13,548 --> 00:52:16,133
I can pay you a higher salary
and incentive pay.

767
00:52:16,926 --> 00:52:18,553
Did you decide to work for him again?

768
00:52:19,679 --> 00:52:22,598
-Yes.
-He must be treating you better, then.

769
00:52:22,682 --> 00:52:23,933
I'm jealous.

770
00:52:25,309 --> 00:52:27,436
Why are you doing this to me, Ms. Lee?

771
00:52:28,855 --> 00:52:30,481
Tell me what you want.

772
00:52:30,565 --> 00:52:32,567
I thought I made myself clear
from the start.

773
00:52:33,150 --> 00:52:34,360
I like you.

774
00:52:35,152 --> 00:52:36,529
I want to be friends.

775
00:52:36,612 --> 00:52:38,990
And I made myself clear from the start.

776
00:52:39,073 --> 00:52:41,993
-I refuse.
-I don't usually make friends with guys.

777
00:52:43,953 --> 00:52:45,413
It's mostly with girls.

778
00:52:51,085 --> 00:52:52,420
I'll head up first.

779
00:52:52,920 --> 00:52:54,338
How cold.

780
00:52:57,258 --> 00:52:58,551
Let's be friends.

781
00:53:01,554 --> 00:53:02,513
No.

782
00:53:02,597 --> 00:53:04,181
I guess I should expose

783
00:53:06,058 --> 00:53:07,518
that you're a woman.

784
00:53:10,062 --> 00:53:11,564
Have fun tricking everyone else.

785
00:53:13,566 --> 00:53:14,692
Have fun tricking what?

786
00:53:18,863 --> 00:53:19,822
Are you curious?

787
00:53:22,909 --> 00:53:24,827
-I mean, Secretary Kang is--
-I'll do it.

788
00:53:26,037 --> 00:53:26,871
Let's be friends.

789
00:53:29,790 --> 00:53:32,251
Tell me. What's this about?

790
00:53:35,504 --> 00:53:36,672
Secretary Kang is…

791
00:53:40,301 --> 00:53:42,345
totally my type.

792
00:53:45,014 --> 00:53:47,183
I was going to do things
behind Yi-jun's back,

793
00:53:47,683 --> 00:53:49,226
but you caught me.

794
00:53:50,519 --> 00:53:52,396
You're too honest,
my future sister-in-law.

795
00:53:52,772 --> 00:53:53,731
And you have guts.

796
00:53:54,982 --> 00:53:57,318
There's no point in lying to you.

797
00:53:58,235 --> 00:53:59,320
He's cute, isn't he?

798
00:54:03,574 --> 00:54:04,700
He is.

799
00:54:06,327 --> 00:54:08,955
If you're going to fool around with him,
do it properly.

800
00:54:10,414 --> 00:54:12,166
Don't worry about it being on the news.

801
00:54:14,043 --> 00:54:16,671
I'd be grateful, but what's in it for you?

802
00:54:17,755 --> 00:54:19,674
Enjoying watching Yi-jun get screwed over?

803
00:54:21,717 --> 00:54:22,802
What a shame.

804
00:54:23,678 --> 00:54:25,221
I think he caught you two

805
00:54:25,763 --> 00:54:26,806
playing around already.

806
00:54:37,108 --> 00:54:39,860
How could you make

807
00:54:40,403 --> 00:54:43,781
someone as worthless as him
your secretary?

808
00:54:44,782 --> 00:54:45,700
Look out.

809
00:54:46,033 --> 00:54:48,244
If your fiancée and your secretary
fool around,

810
00:54:48,661 --> 00:54:50,287
you'll never live it down.

811
00:54:52,331 --> 00:54:54,959
You rolled out a tax hike policy
contrary to expectations.

812
00:54:55,459 --> 00:54:58,963
Don't tell me you used the hotel shares.

813
00:54:59,922 --> 00:55:00,840
It's my hotel.

814
00:55:00,923 --> 00:55:02,883
Try saying that in front of Father.

815
00:55:06,595 --> 00:55:07,513
Aren't you coming?

816
00:55:14,395 --> 00:55:15,896
It's Mom's death anniversary soon.

817
00:55:16,605 --> 00:55:18,691
Why don't you try acting up again?

818
00:55:20,651 --> 00:55:23,237
Things were starting to get fun.
What a disappointment.

819
00:55:23,696 --> 00:55:24,530
Just wait.

820
00:55:26,574 --> 00:55:28,159
The main event

821
00:55:29,827 --> 00:55:31,203
hasn't even started yet.

822
00:55:51,015 --> 00:55:53,601
The police car I saw yesterday
was there again today.

823
00:55:55,227 --> 00:55:57,897
And I saw the security guards
from this morning again tonight.

824
00:55:58,939 --> 00:56:02,943
But why do I have
to report every little thing to you?

825
00:56:03,027 --> 00:56:03,861
First,

826
00:56:04,403 --> 00:56:06,906
you never told me
that you were being followed.

827
00:56:06,989 --> 00:56:10,785
Second, you refused
when I offered to take you home.

828
00:56:10,868 --> 00:56:14,163
Third, your attorney is five minutes away.

829
00:56:15,581 --> 00:56:16,415
Where?

830
00:56:17,917 --> 00:56:19,251
You know exactly where.

831
00:56:23,172 --> 00:56:24,965
I'm bringing dinner,

832
00:56:25,049 --> 00:56:27,384
so go home and clean up if you need to.

833
00:56:49,782 --> 00:56:51,909
I'm not going to let them get in my head.

834
00:56:51,992 --> 00:56:53,410
So you tell me.

835
00:56:55,913 --> 00:56:58,207
Ms. Lee started talking to me first.

836
00:56:58,290 --> 00:57:00,543
-And Ms. Yoon Na-jung--
-I don't care about them!

837
00:57:00,626 --> 00:57:02,086
I'm not interested in those two.

838
00:57:02,795 --> 00:57:05,047
Tell me what's on your mind!
What's the problem?

839
00:57:05,131 --> 00:57:06,298
Why aren't you interested?

840
00:57:07,675 --> 00:57:08,926
She's your fiancée.

841
00:57:09,426 --> 00:57:11,554
You're marrying her.
You should be interested.

842
00:57:11,637 --> 00:57:12,972
She should be your priority.

843
00:57:14,014 --> 00:57:14,849
So that

844
00:57:15,933 --> 00:57:17,560
I don't get the wrong idea.

845
00:57:18,978 --> 00:57:19,812
What?

846
00:57:57,766 --> 00:57:58,684
What is it?

847
00:57:59,393 --> 00:58:00,477
It's nothing.

848
00:58:01,854 --> 00:58:02,938
Let go.

849
00:58:16,118 --> 00:58:17,828
The event is starting soon. It's time…

850
00:58:19,496 --> 00:58:21,165
-What's wrong?
-Everything is fine.

851
00:58:21,624 --> 00:58:23,792
You two go ahead. I'll take care of it.

852
00:58:32,468 --> 00:58:34,011
She's late today.

853
00:58:34,720 --> 00:58:36,138
The light is still turned off.

854
00:58:37,014 --> 00:58:38,515
What's your take, Mr. Profiler?

855
00:58:38,599 --> 00:58:40,601
There may be two reasons for the delay.

856
00:58:40,684 --> 00:58:42,269
There may be outside interference,

857
00:58:44,396 --> 00:58:45,606
or there's a threat inside.

858
00:58:47,775 --> 00:58:48,734
Run.

859
00:59:15,052 --> 00:59:16,220
Mom.

860
00:59:16,762 --> 00:59:18,264
Mom, wake up.

861
00:59:19,807 --> 00:59:22,476
The 2026 Korea Leadership
and Management Awards

862
00:59:23,018 --> 00:59:24,728
will begin with the opening address

863
00:59:24,812 --> 00:59:28,232
by Taekang Group's
Managing Director Yoon Yi-jun.

864
00:59:38,033 --> 00:59:38,867
Hello?

865
00:59:40,494 --> 00:59:41,745
Secretary Lee…

866
00:59:43,122 --> 00:59:45,416
-What did you say?
-Everything is okay there, right?

867
00:59:45,791 --> 00:59:46,959
Everything is fine.

868
00:59:47,042 --> 00:59:49,503
You two go ahead. I'll take care of it.

869
00:59:52,298 --> 00:59:53,382
You're up now, sir.

870
01:00:24,830 --> 01:00:25,998
I have to catch him.

871
01:00:46,393 --> 01:00:47,353
Sir.

872
01:00:51,732 --> 01:00:53,359
Everything went black,

873
01:00:56,528 --> 01:00:58,280
but all I could think about was you.

874
01:01:00,657 --> 01:01:01,742
So for now,

875
01:01:03,994 --> 01:01:05,371
let's just stay like this.

876
01:01:24,807 --> 01:01:26,767
I took advantage of your wish

877
01:01:27,476 --> 01:01:29,019
to have me around for a long time.

878
01:01:31,063 --> 01:01:32,689
But I'll keep taking advantage of it.

879
01:01:33,357 --> 01:01:34,274
So please…

880
01:01:38,612 --> 01:01:39,822
don't come any closer.

881
01:02:10,185 --> 01:02:12,312
SPECIAL THANKS TO
CHOI HEE-JIN AND JUNG YOO-MIN

882
01:02:16,400 --> 01:02:18,193
Wake up, Lee Hye-jung!

883
01:02:18,277 --> 01:02:20,404
-Are you guys crazy?
-Detective Kang has a point.

884
01:02:20,487 --> 01:02:21,405
Did you hit on him?

885
01:02:21,488 --> 01:02:22,990
I had no idea he had such a taste.

886
01:02:23,073 --> 01:02:26,034
-Do you want to go on a blind date?
-Is she pretty?

887
01:02:26,118 --> 01:02:27,119
"Is she pretty"?

888
01:02:27,661 --> 01:02:30,080
Taekang's heir and his male secretary.

889
01:02:30,164 --> 01:02:32,583
Yoon Yi-jun likes you, right?
You know you can't.

890
01:02:32,666 --> 01:02:35,836
You need to face reality first
when you're in danger.

891
01:02:35,919 --> 01:02:37,254
You should've seen it coming.

892
01:02:37,337 --> 01:02:40,382
If I call off my marriage with Si-a,
are you going to like me?

893
01:02:40,466 --> 01:02:41,800
It would never happen.

894
01:02:41,884 --> 01:02:43,051
-I…
-Mr. Yoon!

895
01:02:43,135 --> 01:02:44,428
like you, Kang Jae-hee.

896
01:02:45,679 --> 01:02:48,682
Translated by Leo Chung
